        "AbstractText": "Nutcracker syndrome is rarely seen in the young. Most of the symptoms regress during follow-up. Rarely surgical intervention is necessary. This case presentation is unique for being the first case of nutcracker syndrome and coexistent Cockett syndrome that is treated with surgical intervention."
